WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.670
It's Sunday, November 1, and this is the Microsoft Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.510
Let's catch you up on everything new from Microsoft.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.240
Let's plan ahead with the week's best. For teachers,

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.610
Copilot's Teach is rolling out multi-week unit plans.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:26.720
It lays out the unit week by week, maps your standards and places assessments.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.120
Online parent night?

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:38.140
Teams town halls and webinars are due to get live AI interpretation in December.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:44.560
Messy class lists? Excel's Copilot is rolling out a check for stray spaces,

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:46.360
odd dates and duplicates.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:48.550
Password won't autofill? In Edge,

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:52.260
a right-click Select Password option is due in November.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.770
Two schools, two accounts? From November,

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:58.640
a Teams preview shows both in one window.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.310
Code club or capstone team? GitHub's Teams app is out: tag it,

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:06.740
and Copilot drafts a pull request.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.060
School IT? In November, Frontier previews are due to reach Teams,

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.450
Outlook, OneDrive and SharePoint.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.360
With Foundry's Voice Agent, course notes can become a talking tutor,

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:21.550
using a consented voice and face.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.530
Ransomware plan?

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:28.410
Azure Backup can now restore VM backups into a separate tenant, in preview.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.600
For university data teams, Fabric's Project Osmos agent builds pipelines,

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:37.180
then checks its own results, in preview.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.850
And how does Microsoft test Copilot?

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:44.410
In made-up organisations built from public data, never customer data.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.140
The fine print? A tampered Claude Code extension sat in Cursor's marketplace for hours,

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:51.800
trying to plant a backdoor.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.070
And Targeted release freezes this month,

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:58.270
then retires in January, so review your settings.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:08.130
After hours? Escape Academy 2: Back 2 School joins Game Pass on November 5.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:13.830
Or hunt for over 700 cats in Hidden Cats in Beijing, out November 4.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:20.700
And Football Manager 27's early access starts November 3 on PC Game Pass.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.550
Lessons mapped, previews coming,

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:28.270
a January deadline: good weeks start when you plan ahead.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.350
Zoom out, and it never stops shipping.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.800
Check the board: shipped today, and more on the way.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.690
All of that, in one day. And it keeps on shipping.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.010
You've been watching the Microsoft Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.340
Go build something. See you tomorrow.
